UPDATE blog_posts SET content = E'I write this with tears in my eyes and a fire in my spirit that will not let me stay silent.\n\nI am a theologian who has spent decades buried in the sacred pages of Scripture, but more than that, I am a believer whose heart breaks for every single person reading these words right now. I see you. I see the weight you carry. I see the anxiety that keeps you up at night, the fear that whispers you''re in the wrong place at the wrong time, the exhaustion of trying to control outcomes that were never yours to hold.\n\n## The Weight of Little \"r\" Reality\n\nYou are living in *little r reality*—the narrow, blurry lens of human sight. It is the perspective that says, \"If I don''t make this happen, it won''t happen.\" It is the voice that screams, \"God, where are You?\" while He is quietly, sovereignly, lovingly steering every detail of your life. Little r reality is what the world calls \"normal.\" It is what makes us worry, strive, compare, and collapse under burdens we were never meant to carry.\n\nBut God is calling you—right now—into **Big R Reality**.\n\n---\n\n## Stepping Into Big \"R\" Reality\n\nBig R Reality is not a theory. It is not wishful thinking. It is the actual, living truth of a Father who is in complete control. It is the reality where you can wake up every morning and say with absolute confidence: \"I am exactly where God wants me to be. He is taking me right where I need to go.\"\n\nIt is the realm where anxiety loses its voice because *perfect peace guards your heart and mind* (**Philippians 4:7**). It is the abundant life Jesus promised in **John 10:10**—not a life without trouble, but a life where trouble does not get the final word.\n\nIn Big R Reality, you are never late. You are never behind. You are never forgotten. The same God who parted the Red Sea, who raised Jesus from the dead, who numbers the stars and knows the hairs on your head is personally directing your steps (**Proverbs 3:5-6**). Every detour, every delay, every closed door—He is using it all for your good and His glory (**Romans 8:28**). You are always in the right place at the right time because He is the One who sets the times and seasons (**Acts 1:7**).\n\n---\n\n## How to Make the Shift\n\nHow do we make this shift? Not by trying harder. Not by positive thinking. We do it the way Scripture commands:\n\n> \"Let the word of Christ dwell in you richly…\"\n> **— Colossians 3:16**\n\nNot occasionally. Not when you feel like it. *Richly. Daily. Deeply.* Let it sink into your bones until it becomes the loudest voice in your life.\n\nAnd then pray. Constantly. Honestly. Desperately. Not polished prayers, but the raw cries of a child running to their Father. \"Lord, I''m stuck in little r—pull me into Big R!\" Pray until worry turns to worship, fear turns to faith, and striving turns to rest.\n\n## A Plea to the Adopted Child\n\nI am pleading with you, beloved—right now, as you read this—to stop. Close your eyes for just a moment and whisper:\n\n*\"Father, I surrender my little r lenses. I want Your Big R Reality. Let Your Word dwell richly in me. Teach me to pray without ceasing. I trust You are in control. I receive the abundant life You died to give me.\"*\n\nThis is not a nice suggestion for \"super-spiritual\" Christians. This is the normal Christian life Jesus died to purchase for you. I am pained beyond words to watch so many of God''s precious children living like orphans when they have been adopted as sons and daughters of the King. You were not made to limp through life anxious and exhausted. You were made to walk in the unshakeable confidence that your Father holds the whole world—and your whole story—in His capable, loving hands.\n\n---\n\n## Today is the Day\n\nSo hear this urgent plea from a heart that loves you more than you know: **Today is the day.**\n\nOpen your Bible. Open your mouth in prayer. Refuse to live another moment trapped in little r reality. Step boldly, joyfully, expectantly into the Big R Reality where God is on the throne, where worry has no home, and where *abundant life* is not a future hope but your present reality.\n\nI am praying for you by name right now. You are seen. You are loved. And you are being led—right where you need to go.\n\nWith tears and holy urgency,\n\nA fellow traveler who has tasted Big R Reality and can never go back.\n\n> \"Now may the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, so that by the power of the Holy Spirit you may abound in hope.\"\n> **— Romans 15:13**\n\nWill you join me? Comment below or share this with someone who needs to hear it today. The shift starts now.' WHERE id = '378f2786-bf26-49e6-b56f-9b90c7334ed2';